Desktop drags show only the selected items' icons.

The drag picture was each item as the desktop draws it selected: the
translucent box, the icon and the label over its soft shadow.  On a screen
without a compositing manager a drag's window cannot be partly
transparent; it takes the shape of the opaque part of its picture
instead.  What moved with the pointer was then the box's solid edge and a
ragged label around the icon, where the desktop should show through.

The picture is now the icons alone, where the desktop shows them and as
they look when not selected (a shortcut's mark included), so only the
icons move with the pointer.

